# BEE Timer — Hyprland window rules
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy the block matching your Hyprland version into ~/.config/hypr/hyprland.conf
# (or a file you `source` from it), then run:
#
#     hyprctl reload
#     hyprctl version     # confirm which rule syntax your build understands
#
# Window rules are evaluated when a window OPENS, so restart BEE Timer after
# adding/changing them. On Hyprland 0.57 the runtime commands
# `hyprctl keyword windowrulev2 ...` and `hyprctl keyword windowrule ...`
# both returned "unknown request" — putting the rules in hyprland.conf and
# reloading works. Rule syntax changed around Hyprland 0.53.
#
# The window class is `bee-timer` (the app passes --class=bee-timer).
# Verify with: hyprctl clients
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# === Hyprland <= 0.52: windowrulev2 syntax ================================
windowrulev2 = float,class:^(bee-timer)$
windowrulev2 = size 400 320,class:^(bee-timer)$
windowrulev2 = pin,class:^(bee-timer)$
# Optional: force keyboard focus so Space (pause) always reaches the widget.
# This can steal focus from games/editors — omit it if that is a problem.
windowrulev2 = stayfocused,class:^(bee-timer)$
# Optional: explicit position (absolute layout coordinates; adjust per monitor)
# windowrulev2 = move 1500 40,class:^(bee-timer)$

# === Hyprland 0.53+: windowrule syntax ====================================
# Commas followed by spaces; rule name `stay_focused`.
# windowrule = float, class:^(bee-timer)$
# windowrule = size 400 320, class:^(bee-timer)$
# windowrule = pin, class:^(bee-timer)$
# windowrule = stay_focused, class:^(bee-timer)$
# windowrule = move 1500 40, class:^(bee-timer)$

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Notes
#  * `pin` shows the timer on every workspace. Remove it to keep it on one.
#  * `float` is essential: Hyprland otherwise tiles the 400x320 widget.
#  * Always-on-top comes from the app itself: in the default XWayland mode
#    Hyprland honors _NET_WM_STATE_ABOVE. Native Wayland (BEE_TIMER_OZONE=
#    wayland) has no toplevel always-on-top protocol, so pin + this rule set
#    is your best approximation.
#  * More: docs/HYPRLAND.md in the BEE Timer repository.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
